    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "1c252aa7-4a6b-32ee-86fb-eda0b64184fa",
                "word": "Scouts",
                "pos": "name",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b1537d44-1324-3844-9b81-2b6f226a8451",
                        "entry_id": "1c252aa7-4a6b-32ee-86fb-eda0b64184fa",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A worldwide youth movement with the aim of supporting young people in their physical, mental and spiritual development, so that they may play a constructive role in the society http://www.scout.org/."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a901983a-2d44-4892-ac29-14761b845398",
                                "sense_id": "b1537d44-1324-3844-9b81-2b6f226a8451",
                                "text": "Lord Baden-Powell of England is generally given credit for founding the Scouts. There is no doubt he founded the Scout movement in England along military […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7f6238fe-1351-4539-a725-7cea59ff9f91",
                                "sense_id": "b1537d44-1324-3844-9b81-2b6f226a8451",
                                "text": "In that year Percy Everett suggested that to prevent the Scouts being squeezed out (as they might be if cadet training were to become compulsory for all boys) […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "48af4726-c9d5-422a-9c01-9d4f91587bf0",
                                "sense_id": "b1537d44-1324-3844-9b81-2b6f226a8451",
                                "text": "Boer War hero Robert Baden-Powell founded the Scouts in 1907 so that young men might put military and colonial frontier discipline to work in suburban peacetime."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d9e91348-4514-46a5-9127-7c16e2321e71",
                                "sense_id": "b1537d44-1324-3844-9b81-2b6f226a8451",
                                "text": "Baden-Powell did not himself write animal stories, but when he decided to form an organisation for younger boys, modelled on the Scouts, […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b8a71788-dc14-3b0b-9a03-1d9c1eeb8bd1",
                        "entry_id": "1c252aa7-4a6b-32ee-86fb-eda0b64184fa",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Any of the national Scouts organizations."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "75ac459c-1ac3-4d64-aeb3-6e36211397bc",
                                "sense_id": "b8a71788-dc14-3b0b-9a03-1d9c1eeb8bd1",
                                "text": "The most common criterion of effectiveness quoted from within the Scout Movement is that of the large number of former Scouts who become successful in later [life …]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0a11aea1-826d-4c3d-8372-7ca29676c15c",
                                "sense_id": "b8a71788-dc14-3b0b-9a03-1d9c1eeb8bd1",
                                "text": "The Scouts promise to make a real effort to help Mrs Tuttleby find a Scout group which will appoint her as a leader with a restricted warrant."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d26a8c43-b647-4f80-904d-f0ae30973cb8",
                                "sense_id": "b8a71788-dc14-3b0b-9a03-1d9c1eeb8bd1",
                                "text": "Civic projects were sponsored through service clubs such as Rotary, Apex and Lions. Children might attend Brownies or Cubs, the Guides or the Scouts. […] By the 1960s Australian cultural activities were also being put on an international footing."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d40f44ce-3e7e-47ba-8e61-caaa817537e0",
                                "sense_id": "b8a71788-dc14-3b0b-9a03-1d9c1eeb8bd1",
                                "text": "The Scouts also took him further afield than his native Melbourne. At the end of 1938, he sailed to Sydney for the Scout Jamboree on the Canberra."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a25ef490-c406-4cf5-b03e-b6063d77a30e",
                                "sense_id": "b8a71788-dc14-3b0b-9a03-1d9c1eeb8bd1",
                                "text": "[…] and in 2002, the Guides, Scouts, Returned and Serves League and Surf Life Saving clubs all sponsored Harmony Day."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "57494ad0-1916-4e4d-8850-3af54124fa4f",
                                "sense_id": "b8a71788-dc14-3b0b-9a03-1d9c1eeb8bd1",
                                "text": "[…] wherever I have gone […] I have found companies of Scouts inspired by the true Scout tradition […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d6c8578f-d86b-4fce-a3ba-d5eb58834f32",
                                "sense_id": "b8a71788-dc14-3b0b-9a03-1d9c1eeb8bd1",
                                "text": "[…] in the spring of 1919, a number of local Scouts somehow got hold of a few guns and assisted the Polish soldiers […]\nBesides such common scouting activities as hikes and summer camps, the Scouts participated in various Polish national festivals […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e296310b-9f74-3c76-82d6-90cdb2a28db3",
                        "entry_id": "1c252aa7-4a6b-32ee-86fb-eda0b64184fa",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The Selous Scouts, a special forces regiment of the former Rhodesian Army."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cdf7efa4-455f-4156-a01c-45bc75467b27",
                                "sense_id": "e296310b-9f74-3c76-82d6-90cdb2a28db3",
                                "text": "[…] Turning the tables, the Scouts bit the biter by blowing up […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f7c5e6f7-8196-4f47-b2a1-8d5b09446d96",
                                "sense_id": "e296310b-9f74-3c76-82d6-90cdb2a28db3",
                                "text": "Column strength never exceeded 72 men, and the results achieved were out of all proportion. In alone the Scouts notched up 1,257 kills, only 180 of them internal."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d34c639e-1469-4568-ab3e-4d7eb2f2da66",
                                "sense_id": "e296310b-9f74-3c76-82d6-90cdb2a28db3",
                                "text": "As the terrorists in Rhodesia relied heavily on letters for communication, the Scouts often captured a bonanza of intelligence […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "adbe979c-fd11-4be0-bf13-5b205bea2b00",
                                "sense_id": "e296310b-9f74-3c76-82d6-90cdb2a28db3",
                                "text": "The Scouts recognised that dead CTs were either abandoned or buried and forgotten, whereas the living wounded presented an unwanted burden […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fb0c66a2-b5b6-41f0-a469-1a59529b5a74",
                        "source_entry_id": "1c252aa7-4a6b-32ee-86fb-eda0b64184fa",
